G4396.def:
**προφήτης**, -ου, ὁ [πρόφημι, **to speak forth**),
[in LXX chiefly for נָבִיא ;]
one who acts as an interpreter or forth-teller of the Divine will (see Lft., _Notes_, 83f.; Tr., _Syn._, §vi), **a prophet**;
1. in cl. (Æsch., Hdt., Plat., al.), of the interpreters of oracles.
2. In NT,
(a) **of the OT prophets**: [[Mat.5.12|Mat.5:12]], [[Mrk.6.15|Mrk.6:15]], [[Luk.4.27|Luk.4:27]], [[Jhn.8.52|Jhn.8:52]], [[Rom.11.3|Rom.11:3]], al.;
(b) **of prophets in general**: [[Mat.10.41; 13.57; 21.46|Mat.10:41 13:57 21:46]], [[Mrk.6.4|Mrk.6:4]], [[Luk.13.33|Luk.13:33]], al.;
(with) **of John the Baptist**: [[Mat.21.26|Mat.21:26]], [[Mrk.6.15|Mrk.6:15]], [[Luk.1.76|Luk.1:76]];
(d) **of Christ**: [[Mat.21.11|Mat.21:11]], [[Jhn.6.14|Jhn.6:14]], [[Act.3.22, 23; 7.37|Act.3:22, 23 7:37]]" (LXX) ;
(e) **of Christian prophets in the apostolic age**: [[Act.15.32|Act.15:32]], [[1Co.12.28|1Co.12:28]], [[Eph.2.20|Eph.2:20]], al.;
(f) by meton., of the writings of prophets: [[Luk.24.27|Luk.24:27]], [[Act.8.28|Act.8:28]], al.;
(g) **of a poet**: [[Tit.1.12|Tit.1:12]] (on the use of the term in π. and Inscr., see Deiss., _BS_, 235f.; MM, xxii).
(AS)

G4352.def:
**προσ-κυνέω**, -ῶ
(κυνέω, to kiss), [in LXX chiefly for שָׁחָה hith. ;]
**to make obeisance, do reverence to, worship**;
(a) prop. (as in cl., of the gods: Hdt., Æsch., Plat., al.), of God, **Christ and supra-mundane beings**: absol., [[Jhn.4.20; 12.20|Jhn.4:20 12:20]], [[Act.8.27; 24.11|Act.8:27 24:11]], [[Heb.11.21|Heb.11:21]] (Westc., in l), [[Rev.11.1|Rev.11:1]] πίπτειν καὶ π., [[Rev.5.14|Rev.5:14]] with dative (of the significance of this constr. as com­pared with the usual cl., with accusative, see Abbott, _JG_, 78 f.; _JV_, 133 ff.), [[Jhn.4.21, 23|Jhn.4:21, 23]], [[Act.7.43|Act.7:43]], [[1Co.14.25|1Co.14:25]], [[Heb.1.6|Heb.1:6]], [[Rev.4.10; 7.11; 11.16; 13.4, 15; 14.7; 16.2; 19.4, 10; 19.20; 22.8-9|Rev.4:10 7:11 11:16 13:4, 15 14:7 16:2 19:4, 10 19:20 22:8-9]]; with accusative (see supr.), [[Mat.4.10|Mat.4:10]], [[Luk.4.8; 24.52|Luk.4:8 24:52]] (WH, R, mg., om.), [[Jhn.4.22, 24|Jhn.4:22, 24]], [[Rev.9.20; 13.4, 8; 13.12; 14.9, 11; 20.4|Rev.9:20 13:4, 8 13:12 14:9, 11 20:4]]; Seq. ἐπώπιον, [[Luk.4.7|Luk.4:7]], [[Rev.15.4|Rev.15:4]];
(b) as in cl., of homage to human superiors (cf. MM, xxi): absol., [[Mat.20.20|Mat.20:20]], [[Act.10.25|Act.10:25]]; with dative (see supr.), [[Mat.2.2, 8; 8.2; 9.18; 14.33; 15.25; 18.26; 28.9|Mat.2:2, 8 8:2 9:18 14:33 15:25 18:26 28:9]], [[Mrk.15.19|Mrk.15:19]], [[Jhn.9.38|Jhn.9:38]]; πεσὼν., [[Mat.2.11; 4.9|Mat.2:11 4:9]]; ἐνώπιον τ. ποδῶν, [[Rev.3.9|Rev.3:9]] with accusative, [[Mrk.5.6|Mrk.5:6]] (dative T).†
(AS)

G4314.def:
**πρός**,
_prep. with genitive, dative, accusative_
I. I. C. genitive, of motion from a place, **from the side of**, hence metaphorically, **in the interests of**, [[Act.27.34|Act.27:34]] (cf. Page, in l.).
II. II. C. dative, of local proximity, **hard by, near, at**: [[Mrk.5.11|Mrk.5:11]], [[Luk.19.37|Luk.19:37]], [[Jhn.18.16; 20.11, 12|Jhn.18:16 20:11, 12]] [[Rev.1.13|Rev.1:13]].
III. C. accusative, of motion or direction towards a place or object, **to, towards**.
1. Of place,
(a) **after verbs of motion or of speaking and other words with the idea of direction**: ἔρχομαι, ἀναβαίνω, πορεύομαι, λέγω, ἐπιστολή, etc., [[Mat.3.14|Mat.3:14]], [[Mrk.6.51|Mrk.6:51]], [[Luk.11.5|Luk.11:5]], [[Jhn.2.3|Jhn.2:3]], [[Act.9.2|Act.9:2]], al. mult.; metaphorically, of mental direction, hostile or otherwise, [[Luk.23.12|Luk.23:12]], [[Jhn.6.52|Jhn.6:52]], [[2Co.7.4|2Co.7:4]], [[Eph.6.12|Eph.6:12]], [[Col.3.13|Col.3:13]], al.; of the issue or end, [[Luk.14.32|Luk.14:32]], [[Jhn.11.4|Jhn.11:4]], al.; of purpose, [[Mat.26.12|Mat.26:12]], [[Rom.3.26|Rom.3:26]], [[1Co.6.5|1Co.6:5]], al.; πρὸς τό, with inf., denoting purpose (cf. M, _Pr._, 218, 220; Lft., _Notes_, 131), [[Mat.5.28|Mat.5:28]], [[Mrk.13.22|Mrk.13:22]], [[Eph.6.11|Eph.6:11]], [[1Th.2.9|1Th.2:9]], al.;
(b) of close proximity, **at, by, with**: [[Mat.3.10|Mat.3:10]], [[Mrk.11.4|Mrk.11:4]], [[Luk.4.11|Luk.4:11]], [[Act.3.2|Act.3:2]], al.; after εἶναι, [[Mat.13.56|Mat.13:56]], [[Mrk.6.3|Mrk.6:3]], [[Jhn.1.1|Jhn.1:1]], al.
2. 2. Of time,
(a) **towards** (Plat., Xen., LXX: [[Gen.8.11|Gen.8:11]], al.): [[Luk.24.29|Luk.24:29]];
(b) **for**: πρὸς καιρόν, [[Luk.8.13|Luk.8:13]], [[1Co.7.5|1Co.7:5]]; πρὸς ὥραν, [[Jhn.5.35|Jhn.5:35]], al.; πρὸς ὀλίγον, [[Jas.4.14|Jas.4:14]]
3. Of relation
(a) **toward, with**: [[Rom.5.1|Rom.5:1]], [[2Co.1.12|2Co.1:12]], [[Col.4.5|Col.4:5]], [[1Th.4.12|1Th.4:12]], al.;
(b) **with regard to**: [[Mat.19.8|Mat.19:8]], [[Mrk.12.12|Mrk.12:12]], [[Rom.8.31|Rom.8:31]], al.;
(with) **pertaining to, to**: [[Mat.27.4|Mat.27:4]], [[Jhn.21.22|Jhn.21:22]], [[Rom.15.17|Rom.15:17]], [[Heb.2.17; 5.1|Heb.2:17 5:1]];
(d) **according to**: [[Luk.12.47|Luk.12:47]], [[2Co.5.10|2Co.5:10]], [[Gal.2.14|Gal.2:14]], [[Eph.3.4; 4.14|Eph.3:4 4:14]];
(e) **in comparison with**: [[Rom.8.18|Rom.8:18]]
IV. **In composition**: **towards** (προσέρχομαι), **to** (προσάγω), **against** (προσκόπτω), **besides** (προσδαπανάω) .
(AS)

G4366.def:
**προσ-ρήγνυμι **
[in Aq.: [[Psa.2.9|Psa.2:9]] * ;]
**to break against, dash against**;
(a) trans. (παιδία πέτραις, FlJ, _Ant._, ix, 4, 6);
(b) intrans., with dative: [[Luk.6.48-49|Luk.6:48-49]] (cf. προσπίπτω).†
(AS)
